title: 'benchmarking-cli: drop constant components from per-prefix proof-size analysis'

doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      Fixes `benchmark pallet --output` failing with "Parameter `n` only has 1 unique value(s)"
      for benchmarks touching a storage key only at some component values, e.g. a distinct key
      per item. The per-storage-prefix proof-size analysis now drops components that have a
      single value across the samples touching that prefix, since they determine no slope.
      This applies to every `--analysis` choice. Regenerated weights may change for such keys:
      under `min-squares` with three or more samples, the constant component previously produced
      a spurious slope, and it now contributes a constant.

crates:
  - name: frame-benchmarking-cli
    bump: patch
